  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP Gender Responsive and Integrated Landscape Management in the Ashanti Region of Ghana Initiative Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana&#x2019;s trend of forest loss poses a significant threat to the livelihoods of forest fringe communities, particularly women and the youth, as well as ecosystem services and functionality, that support Ghana&#x2019;s predominantly agrarian economy.In order to address this, the project seeks to build on the significant work that Ghana has already undertaken within its forest landscapes and seeks to integrate lessons and innovation to strengthen climate mitigation and resilience in the forestry sector. Th</narrative>
  </description>
